text:
Pivot after owner review: the first build hand-rolled the reveal
(AnchoredDraggable anchors, parked-open row, two-tap arm) — owner flagged it
against the official docs. Rebuilt on the stock M3 `SwipeToDismissBox`
per developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/touch-input/user-interactions/swipe-to-dismiss:

- delete fires from `confirmValueChange(EndToStart)` — the full swipe past
  the component threshold is the deliberate act; partial swipes spring back;
- `backgroundContent` is empty while `Settled` (the documented pattern —
  WLO rows are transparent over the card);
- the inline undo (where the row was) is the confirmation surface;
- the hand-rolled `WloSwipeRevealRow` in :core:designsystem is deleted;
  no custom swipe primitive ships.
